  "question": {
    "text": "In the circuit shown here, the point &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math>&#39; is kept connected to point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;&#39;&#39; till the current flowing through the circuit becomes constant. Afterward, suddenly, point &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math>&#39; is disconnected from point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> &#39;&#39; and connected to point &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&#39; at time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. Ratio of the voltage across resistance and the inductor at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mi>R</mi></mfrac></math> will be equal to :<br /><br />&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/EM0025741_Question.jpg\" style=\"width: 242px; height: 130px;\" />",
    "image": null
  },
